   "source": [
    "# Tier 8 â€” Expert integration & the MCP-facing API\n",
    "\n",
    "The capstone. Two ideas:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **One results contract.** BioSTEAM and QSDsan share the same `System`/`TEA`/\n",
    "   `Model` base classes, so a *single* `summarize_system` function works across\n",
    "   frameworks and across models â€” from a toy flowsheet to a published biorefinery.\n",
    "2. That contract is exactly what the **MCP server** (Phase 3) returns. Designing it\n",
    "   here, against the real API, is what makes the MCP spec trustworthy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "8ff8c6e8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-12T11:58:10.033187Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-12T11:58:10.033187Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.420348Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.419252Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import biosteam as bst"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "204bd5e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. A uniform results contract\n",
    "\n",
    "`summarize_system` takes a simulated system (and optional TEA + product) and returns\n",
    "a plain, JSON-friendly dict. Plain dict = trivially serializable over MCP."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "fa064f3f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.426540Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.425781Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.440827Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-12T11:58:24.439836Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def summarize_system(system, tea=None, product=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return a JSON-friendly summary of a simulated BioSTEAM/QSDsan system.\"\"\"\n",
    "    summary = {\n",
    "        \"system\": system.ID,\n",
    "        \"n_units\": len(system.units),\n",
    "        \"units\": [u.ID for u in system.units],\n",
    "        \"installed_equipment_cost_MM\": round(system.installed_equipment_cost / 1e6, 3),\n",
    "        \"feeds\": {s.ID: round(s.F_mass, 1) for s in system.feeds},\n",
    "        \"products\": {s.ID: round(s.F_mass, 1) for s in system.products},\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if tea is not None:\n",
    "        summary[\"tea\"] = {\n",
    "            \"FCI_MM\": round(tea.FCI / 1e6, 3),\n",
    "            \"FOC_MM_per_yr\": round(tea.FOC / 1e6, 3),\n",
    "            \"VOC_MM_per_yr\": round(tea.VOC / 1e6, 3),\n",
    "            \"NPV_MM\": round(tea.NPV / 1e6, 2),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        if product is not None:\n",
    "            summary[\"tea\"][\"MSP_usd_per_kg\"] = round(float(tea.solve_price(product)), 4)\n",
    "    return summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "713e0231",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Apply it to a published biorefinery\n",
    "\n",
    "The `biorefineries` package ships peer-reviewed BioSTEAM models. Load cornstoverâ†’\n",
    "ethanol and summarize it through the *same* contract â€” no bespoke extraction code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
